
-- fallbacks.pgm - Conversation Recovery & Unknown Input Handler Component
-- Essential component for graceful degradation and conversation flow management
-- Covers misunderstanding recovery, clarification requests, and conversation continuity

-- Generic Misunderstanding
Recognizer "I don't understand"
	Remember "Bot didn't understand user"
	Option Say "I'm not quite following. Could you try rephrasing that?"
	Option Say "I didn't catch that. Can you say it differently?"

Recognizer "what"
	Remember "User said what"
	Option Say "Sorry, what would you like to know?"
	Option Say "What specifically can I help you with?"

Recognizer "huh"
	Remember "User expressed confusion"
	Option Say "I can see this might be confusing. What would help clarify things?"
	Option Say "Let me try to be clearer. What are you wondering about?"

-- Clarification Requests
Recognizer "could you clarify"
	Remember "User needs clarification"
	Option Say "Absolutely! What part would you like me to explain more clearly?"
	Option Say "Of course! What needs more explanation?"

Recognizer "I'm not sure what you mean"
	Remember "User doesn't understand bot"
	Option Say "Let me try explaining that differently. What was unclear?"
	Option Say "I should be clearer. What didn't make sense?"

Recognizer "that doesn't make sense"
	Remember "User thinks bot doesn't make sense"
	Option Say "You're right, let me try a different approach. What's confusing?"
	Option Say "That's fair. Let me explain it better. What part isn't clear?"

-- Conversation Recovery
Recognizer "nevermind"
	Remember "User wants to drop topic"
	Option Say "No problem at all! Is there something else I can help you with?"
	Option Say "That's totally fine! What else is on your mind?"

Recognizer "forget it"
	Remember "User wants to abandon topic"
	Option Say "Sure thing! Let's move on. What would you like to talk about?"
	Option Say "No worries! Is there anything else I can help with?"

Recognizer "start over"
	Remember "User wants to start fresh"
	Option Say "Absolutely! Let's begin again. What can I help you with?"
	Option Say "Fresh start sounds great! What would you like to do?"

-- Alternative Suggestions
Recognizer "I don't know what to ask"
	Remember "User needs conversation suggestions"
	Option Say "That's totally normal! You could ask me about any topic you're curious about."
	Option Say "No pressure! Feel free to share anything on your mind, or ask about something you're interested in."

Recognizer "what should I say"
	Remember "User needs interaction help"
	Option Say "You can ask me anything! Try asking about a topic you're curious about."
	Option Say "Just be yourself! Ask about something you're wondering about or tell me what's on your mind."

Recognizer "what can you do"
	Remember "User asks about capabilities"
	Option Say "I'm here to chat and help however I can! What kind of assistance are you looking for?"
	Option Say "I love conversations on all kinds of topics! What interests you most?"

-- Error Acknowledgment
Recognizer "that's wrong"
	Remember "User says bot is wrong"
	Option Say "I appreciate you pointing that out! What should I understand differently?"
	Option Say "Thank you for the correction! Can you help me understand the right way?"

Recognizer "that's not right"
	Remember "User corrects bot"
	Option Say "You're absolutely right to correct me! What's the accurate information?"
	Option Say "Thanks for setting me straight! What should I know instead?"

Recognizer "you're confused"
	Remember "User thinks bot is confused"
	Option Say "I might be! Can you help me understand what I'm missing?"
	Option Say "You could be right! What would help me get on the right track?"

-- Conversation Flow
Recognizer "anyway"
	Remember "User wants to change topic"
	Option Say "Sure! What's next on your mind?"
	Option Say "What else would you like to talk about?"

Recognizer "moving on"
	Remember "User switching topics"
	Option Say "Sounds good! What would you like to discuss?"
	Option Say "Perfect! What's next?"

Recognizer "different topic"
	Remember "User wants topic change"
	Option Say "Absolutely! What new topic interests you?"
	Option Say "Great idea! What would you like to explore?"

-- Engagement Recovery
Recognizer "this is boring"
	Remember "User finds conversation boring"
	Option Say "Let's make this more interesting! What would you enjoy talking about?"
	Option Say "I hear you! What topic would be more engaging for you?"

Recognizer "you're boring"
	Remember "User finds bot boring"
	Option Say "Fair point! What would make our conversation more interesting?"
	Option Say "I can do better! What kind of conversation would you prefer?"

Recognizer "whatever"
	Remember "User seems disengaged"
	Option Say "I sense you might be losing interest. What would make this more worthwhile?"
	Option Say "Let's find something you care about! What matters to you right now?"

-- Repetition Handling
Recognizer "you already said that"
	Remember "Bot repeated itself"
	Option Say "You're absolutely right! Let me try a different approach."
	Option Say "Good catch! Let me give you something new instead."

Recognizer "we talked about this"
	Remember "Topic already discussed"
	Option Say "True! Should we explore a different angle or move to something else?"
	Option Say "You're right! What new direction should we take?"

-- Technical Difficulties
Recognizer "you're not working"
	Remember "User experiencing technical issues"
	Option Say "I'm sorry you're having trouble! Let's try starting fresh. What can I help with?"
	Option Say "That's frustrating! Let me try to be more helpful. What do you need?"

Recognizer "broken"
	Remember "User thinks something is broken"
	Option Say "Sorry for any confusion! Let's try a different approach. What are you trying to do?"
	Option Say "Let me try to work better! What would help?"

-- Encouragement to Continue
Recognizer "I give up"
	Remember "User wants to give up"
	Option Say "Don't give up! Sometimes these things take a moment to click. What's the main challenge?"
	Option Say "I understand it can be frustrating! What would make this easier?"

Recognizer "this is hard"
	Remember "User finds interaction difficult"
	Option Say "You're doing fine! What would make this feel easier?"
	Option Say "Hard things are often worth it! What's the trickiest part?"

Recognizer "I'm lost"
	Remember "User feels lost in conversation"
	Option Say "Let's get you back on track! What were you hoping to accomplish?"
	Option Say "No problem! Let's take it step by step. What's your main question?"

-- Silence Breakers
Recognizer "umm"
	Remember "User hesitating"
	Option Say "Take your time! What's on your mind?"
	Option Say "No rush! What would you like to talk about?"

Recognizer "uh"
	Remember "User uncertain"
	Option Say "It's okay to think it through! What are you considering?"
	Option Say "What's coming to mind?"

Recognizer "hmm"
	Remember "User pondering"
	Option Say "I can see you're thinking! What's percolating?"
	Option Say "Thinking is good! What's on your mind?"

-- Conversation Starters
Recognizer "I'm bored"
	Remember "User is bored"
	Option Say "Let's fix that! What kind of things usually interest you?"
	Option Say "Boredom is just potential waiting to be unlocked! What sounds fun?"

Recognizer "entertain me"
	Remember "User wants entertainment"
	Option Say "I'd love to! What kind of entertainment appeals to you right now?"
	Option Say "Let's have some fun! What would be entertaining for you?"

Recognizer "surprise me"
	Remember "User wants surprise"
	Option Say "I love surprises! What kind of surprise would delight you most?"
	Option Say "Surprises are the best! What area should I surprise you about?"

-- Meta-conversation
Recognizer "how do I talk to you"
	Remember "User needs interaction guidance"
	Option Say "Just talk naturally! Ask questions, share thoughts, or tell me what's on your mind."
	Option Say "Be yourself! I respond to questions, comments, and conversation just like talking to a friend."

Recognizer "what should we talk about"
	Remember "User wants topic suggestions"
	Option Say "We could talk about anything you're curious about! What interests you lately?"
	Option Say "The best conversations start with what matters to you! What's been on your mind?"

Recognizer "is this working"
	Remember "User checking if conversation is working"
	Option Say "I think so! How does it feel to you? What would make it better?"
	Option Say "Seems like it! What would make this conversation work better for you?"

